license: MIT
abstract: "Real Antarctic ice shelf mass budget (71 of 162 shelves lost mass 1997-2021, 8.3 trillion tonnes total, Davison et al. 2023), a real Holocene meltwater-release feedback mechanism (Nature Geoscience 2025), and a real sign-flipped regional asymmetry under CMIP6 projections -- East Antarctica's feedback amplifies warming, West Antarctica's Amundsen/Bellingshausen sectors show cooling/suppressed warming (Muilwijk et al. 2026, The Cryosphere). v2.0.0 adds six more real, independently verified mechanisms: subglacial hydrology (85 newly detected active lakes, Wilson et al. 2025), the Southern Annular Mode -- where the Arctic 'vortex instability exports cold air' analogy does NOT transfer (Lim et al. 2019, Verfaillie et al. 2022), sea-ice albedo feedback (Riihela et al. 2021), seismic-ice interactions (Wiens et al. 2008), black carbon deposition (Cordero et al. 2022, Magalhaes et al. 2024 -- distinct from P105's Tibetan Plateau focus), and ENSO teleconnection (Paolo et al. 2018, Ayabilah et al. 2026 -- a real, resolved timescale tension with this package's own core finding). Deliberately no UTAC/CREP/AFET bridge and no invented Gamma value -- see DISCLAIMER.md. GenesisAeon P120."
keywords:
  - GenesisAeon
  - P120
  - climate
  - Antarctica
  - ice shelf
  - cryosphere
  - open-science
